\# Threadline Monthly Strategy Report

\#\# 1\. Action  
What Threadline actually did this month. Keep it brief and auditable.  
\- assets shipped / channels / experiments;  
\- research and strategy actions;  
\- production/recording improvements;  
\- conversion/tracking actions implemented.

\#\# 2\. Results  
Separate results into four layers.

\#\#\# A. Operational  
\- Founder hours on content vs baseline.  
\- Core output/consistency.  
\- Production cycle time.  
\- Approval turnaround.  
\- Revision/coordination burden.

\#\#\# B. Attention  
\- Views/reach where relevant.  
\- Retention/watch time.  
\- Saves/shares/comments.  
\- Profile visits and audience-quality signals.  
These are leading indicators, not ROI by themselves.

\#\#\# C. Commercial Intent  
\- Tracked link clicks.  
\- Opt-ins.  
\- DMs/enquiries.  
\- Booked calls.

\#\#\# D. Commercial Outcome  
\- Qualified opportunities.  
\- Pipeline value.  
\- Closed-won revenue where observable.  
\- Buyer-named content influence.

For every commercial figure, label evidence/attribution:  
DIRECTLY\_TRACKED / BUYER\_NAMED\_CLIENT\_ATTRIBUTED / MULTI\_TOUCH\_INFLUENCED / ASSOCIATED\_CORRELATED / QUALITATIVE\_ONLY.  
Also mark MEASURED vs CLIENT-REPORTED and show first-touch / last-touch separately where supported.

\#\# Tracking-health note  
Before interpreting results, show whether the measurement system is complete:  
\- baseline captured;  
\- asset/content IDs \+ live URLs current;  
\- tracked-link/UTM coverage;  
\- CRM source capture;  
\- booking-source question active;  
\- last platform-metric refresh;  
\- last weekly Commercial Signal Capture;  
\- known data gaps.

\#\# Commercial efficiency metrics — only when data quality supports them  
\- booked calls per 10,000 views;  
\- qualified opportunities per 10,000 views;  
\- qualified pipeline per 10,000 views;  
\- revenue per asset;  
\- revenue per 1,000 views;  
\- commercial value by topic/pillar/CTA.  
Do not present monetary efficiency if attribution coverage is weak.

\#\# 3\. Problems  
\- Current constraint.  
\- What underperformed and why we think it did.  
\- Missing inputs / blockers.  
\- Tracking gaps or weak attribution.  
\- What evidence is weak or ambiguous.

\#\# 4\. Future  
\- 3–5 ranked market/content findings.  
\- Recommended content tests.  
\- What we will stop, continue and change.  
\- Any tracking fixes needed.  
\- What we need from the client.

\#\# Attribution language  
Use “tracked from”, “buyer named”, “influenced”, “associated with”, “reported after”, or “commercial signal” as appropriate. Do not claim Threadline caused a business outcome unless the evidence genuinely supports causality.  
